# busybox init, and three lines of it. There is no service manager in this
# guest on purpose: what it has to bring up is a udev, a dbus, the agent and an
# X server, and that is a script rather than a dependency graph.
#
# The console is ttyS0 and goes to the container's log; ttyS1 is a shell for
# somebody debugging by hand, and it is a socket the host connects to rather
# than a file, so a getty with nobody on the other end waits instead of
# respawning.
::sysinit:/sbin/guest-init
::respawn:/sbin/getty -n -l /bin/sh -L 115200 ttyS1 vt100
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
